# Everything the build does not need, and two things it must never have.
#
# `.env` holds the model keys. A key copied into a layer is published to whoever can pull the image,
# and `docker history` shows it even after a later layer deletes the file. Keys arrive as environment
# at run time or they do not arrive.
#
# `evals/` and the corpus are state. Baking a 1.2 GB database into an image means rebuilding it to
# ingest one judgment.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github
.venv
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

tests
docs
demo
evals
scripts
infra
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.md
!README.md

# Anything that looks like a corpus or a model, wherever it landed.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3-*
*.npy
*.jsonl
